@@ -70,6 +70,24 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to :meth:`~rich.console.Console.print` and :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log`. It converts each object to a string with ``str()``, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result as plain text followed by ``end``. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("foo", "bar", sep="-", end="!")
+
+``out`` does the following:
+
+* Writes the objects as raw text, without pretty printing containers such as dicts and lists.
+* Does not word wrap or crop the output, so long lines run on as they are.
+* Does not interpret :ref:`console_markup` or replace emoji codes.
+* Applies highlighting by default. Pass ``highlight=False`` to turn it off, or ``highlight=None`` to use the Console's own highlight setting.
+* Applies a basic ``style`` if one is given.
+
+Use ``out`` when you want the text written exactly as you supply it. Use :meth:`~rich.console.Console.print` when you want pretty printing, wrapping, or markup.
+
+
